<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bhanja dynasty</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Bhanja dynasty is a ruling family of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odisha">Odisha</a> in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, known from early medieval inscriptions and claiming ancient descent. Branches ruled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/princely-state">princely states</a> of Mayurbhanj and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kendujhar">Keonjhar</a>, and related lines held other small states in Odisha, until these merged into the Indian Union in 1948–1949.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bhanja-dynasty.jpg" alt="Bhanja dynasty" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Takshashila7977 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_of_Bengal_in_958_CE.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
